78:- `nexus triggers release <id> [-w <workspace>] [--limiter]`: clear a trigger's quarantine. Like `approve` it needs a person at a terminal and the exact word `yes`. It does not write the limiter itself: it leaves a request file the runner applies within seconds (or at its next start), so the runner is the only writer of the limiter state. It does not clear a rate window (the cap still applies) and it does not approve anything. `--limiter` also unlocks the whole limiter after its stored state was refused (below).
